# Making a CSS Grid Layout Responsive for Mobile Devices

To modify a CSS grid layout for mobile responsiveness, you can use these approaches:

## 1. Media Queries
```css
.grid-container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  gap: 20px;
}

/* Mobile devices */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .grid-container {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 10px;
  }
}

/* Small mobile devices */
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .grid-container {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
```

## 2. Use auto-fill or auto-fit
```css
.grid-container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(250px, 1fr));
  gap: 20px;
}
```

## 3. Use minmax() for flexible column widths
```css
.grid-container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(150px, 1fr));
  gap: 20px;
}
```

## 4. Grid areas for layout reorganization
```css
.grid-container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-areas: 
    "header header header"
    "sidebar content content"
    "footer footer footer";
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .grid-container {
    grid-template-areas: 
      "header"
      "sidebar"
      "content"
      "footer";
  }
}
```

Don't forget to add the viewport meta tag in your HTML:
```html
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
